# RNNoise vendored inference sources

Veylo uses RNNoise v0.2 at commit
`904a876dce1f9ab8860c0a5000ed151f9f6eef58` from
[the official source](https://github.com/xiph/rnnoise/tree/904a876dce1f9ab8860c0a5000ed151f9f6eef58).
Only the C inference sources, required headers, default generated model and
license/author notices are retained here. Build them through Veylo's root
`CMakeLists.txt`; this directory is not a standalone Autotools project.

The runtime model is `src/rnnoise_data.c` with `src/rnnoise_data.h`.
Veylo does not load a PyTorch checkpoint. Training scripts, the `.pth` training
checkpoint, model-export tools and the optional smaller model are available
from the pinned upstream source and model archive instead of this repository.
`dependencies.lock.json` retains their upstream source/model archive checksums
and hashes every retained dependency file.

Veylo retains two local patches: OSXSAVE/XCR0 checks before AVX2/FMA selection
and the transient energy gain-decay backport. See `THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md` at the
repository root. Original license and author notices remain in `COPYING`,
`AUTHORS` and source headers.

RNNoise's algorithm is described in J.-M. Valin, *A Hybrid DSP/Deep Learning
Approach to Real-Time Full-Band Speech Enhancement*, MMSP 2018,
[arXiv:1709.08243](https://arxiv.org/abs/1709.08243).
